post.description:
Creates an asynchronous bulk PAN verification job for the supplied TAN. The response contains a job ID and a signed URL for the input JSON workbook. Upload the workbook with HTTP PUT and Content-Type application/json.

Save the [TRACES credentials](https://developer.sandbox.co.in/api-reference/tds/compliance/traces-credentials/endpoints/save_credential) for the TAN before processing. Credential checks happen after the workbook upload. Missing or incorrect credentials appear as a failed job when you retrieve its status.

The uploaded JSON file must be at most 5,000,000 bytes. The workbook contains payee_sheet and payee_table with the header ["sr_no", "pan"]. Missing or malformed PAN values fail workbook validation. For repeated PANs, verification keeps the first row and ignores later rows.

Retrieve the job with the returned job_id to check progress and obtain the output download URL.

Input workbook example:

```json
{
  "@entity": "workbook",
  "name": "pan_verification_workbook",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "@entity": "sheet",
      "name": "payee_sheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "@entity": "table",
          "name": "payee_table",
          "header": [
            "sr_no",
            "pan"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              1,
              "ABCPD1234E"
            ],
            [
              2,
              "XYZPK5678L"
            ],
            [
              3,
              "ABCPD1234E"
            ],
            [
              4,
              "AAAAA1111A"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
